  "id": "COMPOUND:11153 - PROTEIN:5864",
  "verbalization": "Propamidine is implicated in the biological activity of U373 MG through a series of interconnected pathways, with the target of Propamidine being a family of enzymes, including Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like and Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9. These enzymes are involved in the metabolism of various compounds, with the 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside acting as intermediates in the metabolic cascade. The final link in this chain is U373 MG, a cell line that is sensitive to these metabolic products. The evidence suggests that Propamidine may exert its effects by modulating the activity of these enzymes, which in turn influence the metabolic pathways that lead to the activation of U373 MG. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Propamidine could interact with U373 MG, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
